  {
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "body": "@atalman Do we have any document/notiion on what should/should not be included in `https://download.pytorch.org/whl/torch`?   (I remember seeing an issue long time ago about those `+foobar` suffixes and how they are incompatible with some versions of potery/UV\n\nI.e. following should work\n```\npip3.11 install --no-cache-dir --find-links https://download.pytorch.org/whl/cu124/torch/ torch==2.6.0\n```\nAnd indeed saying that one wants to download something from `https://download.pytorch.org/whl/torch/` is ambigous (and perhaps we should slap a big warning on the index about it)",
